[PROVED/SYMBOLIC] seed spinor
D=f_xx-f_yy=cos(2x)+(6/5)cos(2y)-(1/2)cos(4y)
C=2f_xy=2cos(x)cos(y)
min_R2 (D^2+C^2)=49/2500; hence min |f_barwbarw|=7/200
seed phase has winding zero on every closed plane loop
[PROVED/SYMBOLIC] polynomial Hessian spinor gate
q_+ q_-=(Delta H)^2-4 det(Hess H)
circle Laurent support for deg(q)<=D lies in [-D,D], so |wind(q)|<=D
therefore a degree-d Hessian carrier has |line-index|<=(d-2)/2
matching index 1+k/2 requires d>=k+4 (necessary, not sufficient)
[PROVED/SYMBOLIC over Q] quadratic-u conductor-square nodal cell
universe: deg_u(h,k,z,w)<=2; conductor order<=2; no coefficient-height cap
ordered-field gates force h2=k2=0, then h1=k1=0, then z2=w2=0
[X^3 u^12]O=-54(h2^4+6h2^2k2^2+k2^4)
[X^3 u^8]O=-54(h1^4+6h1^2k1^2+k1^4) after h2=k2=0
[X^3 u^6]O=-24(z2^2+w2^2) after h1=k1=h2=k2=0
successive square gates force w1=-3h0k0, z1=-3(h0^2+k0^2)/2,
w0=-3h0/4, z0=-3k0/4
terminal residual [X^2 u^0](E-1)=-87/32
controls: generic first-layer solve PASS; p->p+1 hostile REJECTED
period cross-check: closed coefficient pairing == direct exact t-moments
period defect=2(4h0^2+4h0k0+64k0^3u+28k0^2-35)/35
period on the collapsed cell forces k0=0, h0^2=35/4: no Q-point
scope: definite quartics/sums of squares use Q/order; no complex no-go claimed
